# State Management: Zustand

## Where state lives

| State type        | Location                              |
|-------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Feature UI state  | `features/[name]/store/[name]Store.ts`|
| Global UI state   | `shared/lib/zustand.ts`               |
| Server/async data | React Query — NOT Zustand             |

## Store slice pattern

```ts
// features/[name]/store/[name]Store.ts
import { create } from 'zustand'
import { devtools } from 'zustand/middleware'

interface [Name]State {
  // state fields
  // actions (set*)
}

export const use[Name]Store = create<[Name]State>()(
  devtools(
    (set, get) => ({
      // initial state
      // actions
    }),
    { name: '[name]-store' }
  )
)
```

## Rules

- Always wrap with `devtools()` for Redux DevTools support
- Use `immer` middleware for complex nested state updates
- Never store server data (API responses) in Zustand — use React Query
- Never call Zustand stores directly in components — wrap in a feature hook first:

```ts
// features/auth/hooks/useSession.ts  ← wrap the store
export const useSession = () => {
  const user = useAuthStore((s) => s.user)
  const setUser = useAuthStore((s) => s.setUser)
  return { user, setUser, isAuthenticated: !!user }
}
```

- Select only what you need (avoid `useStore(s => s)` — causes re-renders):

```ts
// GOOD
const user = useAuthStore((s) => s.user)

// BAD
const { user, setUser, ...rest } = useAuthStore()
```
